    "granted_by": "Maintainer decision, 2026-08-21, at commit f331e49. GO for Phase-A Attempt 12 only. Attempt 11 passed Stage 0 and Stage 1 -- the first completed AutoInit beam search, 43 states over 4 levels, five leaves selected, with the existing COMPOSITE_STAGE1 recipe on Pareto front 4 and NOT selected -- and then lost the probe at Stage 2 to a tokenizer inferred from a weight-only checkpoint, and lost all five leaf checkpoints with the pod. Both defects are closed and mutation-verified at $0. (1) The tokenizer is now a declared consumer dependency: an explicit source, loaded through the real loader, verified against the frozen protocol identity 7781771acc3798ee, cross-checked against any tokenizer the student itself carries, and refused before training or data construction; presence is decided by looking for files, never by calling the loader, because AutoTokenizer returns a one-token vocabulary on a config-only directory instead of raising. The producer is unchanged and searched leaves remain weight-only, because artifact_digest folds in tokenizer_sha256. (2) The five Stage-1 selected leaves now leave the pod: selected_leaf_durability.json is a fetched report ordered before products, the selected-leaf transfer runs whenever Stage 1 produced that report and is NOT gated on Stage 2, the leaves land in the existing dev-box checkpoint store by the product transfer path rather than the archive, each is re-identified from local bytes and required to match the Stage-1 artifact digest, and required_products_secured is a teardown-gate requirement so a completed search cannot be deleted while its leaves remain only on the pod. A pre-provider capacity gate now checks the actual dev-box destination. Local storage was cleared to 22.25 GiB by reclaiming 14.9107 GiB of derived caches with no checkpoint deleted; the retained 23.09 GiB review set is closed and must not be revisited. No further canary, measurement, readiness or cleanup phase is to be added before this run.\n\nCovers: One (1) launch of AutoInitializer Phase A, attempt 12, on a single NVIDIA L40S at no more than $0.99/h, proceeding through the frozen Stage 0-5 protocol with no scientific or infrastructure change, under the existing watchdog, soft-stop, hard-stop, artifact-gate, selected-leaf durability and provider-confirmed teardown behaviour. Authorized pricing, unchanged: expected $17.8933, soft stop $22.7183, priced hard value $23.0483, per-launch hard ceiling $23.0484. Stage-1 runtime deadline 363.9841 min, derived as base 180.0000 + beam-6 correction 36.2158 + reference-cache fallback reserve 147.7683. If Stage 1 completes, all five selected leaves MUST be verified off-pod before normal teardown, whatever happens in Stages 2-5.\n\nCumulative spend at approval $209.6842 against a cumulative cap of $234.00.\n\nDoes NOT authorize: Attempt 13, or any retry after a failure - a failed pre-provider, capacity, setup, Stage-0, Stage-1, Stage-2, Stage-3, pricing, authorization, bundle-identity, deadline, selected-leaf-durability, artifact or provider gate is a fail-closed stop for review, never an interactive repair on the live pod. Adding a further canary, measurement, readiness or cleanup phase. Deleting any further local artifact, or revisiting the retained 23.09 GiB checkpoint review set. Changing the tokenizer semantics, the search science, the retention selection, the five-leaf count, or Phase-A pricing. Reopening the frozen science: science plan 02be33b9, session plan 9377a2dc, Stage-3 protocol 250f72ef, runtime comparability 70a26e0b, equivalence interval 0.011695296982299022, feasibility floor 0.3, the seed and conditional-sc policy, the operators, the calibration, the operator ids and declared mathematics, or the recovery, search and selection rules. Reviving the terminated device canary. Any other paid session. Treating the remaining cumulative headroom as authorization beyond this one launch.\n\nGrant document: logs/autoinit_phase_a_attempt12_grant.json sha256 69e